INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'upessc-prt-assistant-teacher-12405-posts-20261103', 'global', 'India',
'UPESSC PRT Recruitment 2026: 12,405 Assistant Teacher Posts, Last Date 4 November',
'',
'UPESSC Assistant Teacher (Primary) applications for 12,405 posts close on 4 November 2026 after a court-ordered extension, with corrections open until 7 November 2026 and the written examination on 3 and 4 December 2026.',
'',
$$<p>On 3 November 2026, the Uttar Pradesh Education Service Selection Commission (UPESSC) reminded applicants that time has almost run out for one of the largest teacher recruitments of the year: the <a href="https://www.jagranjosh.com/lite/articles/upessc-prt-recruitment-2026-last-date-apply-online-for-assistant-teacher-posts-check-eligibility-and-direct-link-1800018575-1">UPESSC PRT recruitment 2026 for 12,405 Assistant Teacher (Primary) posts</a> closes on 4 November 2026. The last date to apply was extended to 4 November 2026 after an Allahabad High Court order of 24 October 2026, and the commission has said the correction window stays open until 7 November 2026, with the written examination unchanged on 3 and 4 December 2026. Candidates who have not yet applied should complete the form and pay the fee before the deadline, because the commission's own advice warns that the website can become slow in the final hours.</p>
<p>The eligibility limits should be checked before the form, not after it. The applicant must be an Indian citizen, hold graduation plus a teacher-training diploma (D.El.Ed or D.L.Ed) from an NCTE-recognised programme, and have passed the Teacher Eligibility Test at the primary level, either UPTET or CTET for classes 1 to 5. The minimum age is 21 years, calculated as on 1 July 2026, with a maximum age of 40 years for Assistant Teacher (Primary, Urban) and 62 years for Assistant Teacher (Attached Primary), and age relaxation for reserved categories under UPESSC and Uttar Pradesh government rules. Two qualifications were newly added under this advertisement: the two-year Diploma in Education (Special Education) approved by the Rehabilitation Council of India, and the four-year B.El.Ed. Candidates holding those qualifications, who may have been unsure of their standing earlier in the process, are named in the latest update as eligible to apply.</p>
<h2>UPESSC PRT recruitment 2026: at a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Organisation</th><td>Uttar Pradesh Education Service Selection Commission (UPESSC), Prayagraj</td></tr>
<tr><th>Post</th><td>Assistant Teacher (Associated Primary), Secondary Education Department</td></tr>
<tr><th>Advertisement number</th><td>05/2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Total vacancies</th><td>12,405</td></tr>
<tr><th>Last date to apply</th><td>4 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Last date for application correction</th><td>7 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Written examination dates</th><td>3 and 4 December 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application mode</th><td>Online only, through upessc.up.gov.in</td></tr>
<tr><th>Essential qualifications</th><td>Graduation plus D.El.Ed or D.L.Ed, and a primary-level TET pass (UPTET or CTET)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Newly added qualifications</th><td>Two-year Diploma in Education (Special Education) approved by the Rehabilitation Council of India, and four-year B.El.Ed</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>As stated in the main advertisement; not restated in the deadline update</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Why the deadline moved, and why it will not move again on its own</h2>
<p>The extension to 4 November 2026 followed an Allahabad High Court order of 24 October 2026, and that origin matters for how candidates should treat the date. A court-directed extension is not a rolling grace period: the commission has fixed the last date, fixed the correction window, and left the examination dates unchanged, which signals that the schedule from here is set. Candidates who assume a further extension will appear are gambling with a recruitment of 12,405 posts, and the cost of losing that gamble is a full cycle of waiting. The correction window to 7 November 2026 gives applicants room to fix errors, but it is not a second application window, and it does not rescue a form that was never submitted.</p>
<p>The scale of this recruitment is what makes it stand out. Twelve thousand four hundred and five primary teacher posts in a single advertisement is a rare opening for trained primary teachers, and it sits alongside the commission's <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/upessc-principal-headmaster-2647-posts-20261025">other large teacher recruitments</a> this year, including the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/upessc-tgt-17735-posts-20261025">Trained Graduate Teacher posts</a> covered earlier on this site. Primary teaching in Uttar Pradesh's secondary education department carries a different profile from secondary teaching: the classroom is classes 1 to 5, the qualifying test is the primary-level TET, and the training qualification is the diploma route rather than a postgraduate degree. For D.El.Ed and B.El.Ed holders, this is the recruitment their qualification was built for, and the newly added Special Education diploma widens the field further for candidates trained to teach children with special needs.</p>
<h2>How to apply before 4 November 2026</h2>
<p>Apply only through the official website, upessc.up.gov.in, using the application link for Advertisement No. 05/2026, PRT Assistant Teacher (Associated Primary). The steps are: register with name, mobile number and email address if not already registered; log in with the credentials received; fill in personal, educational and category details carefully; select the qualification held, including the newly added Diploma in Special Education or B.El.Ed where applicable; upload the photograph, signature and other documents in the prescribed format; pay the application fee online as stated in the main advertisement; review the form; and submit. Download the confirmation page and keep a printout for future use.</p>
<p>Three practical points deserve emphasis. First, check the TET condition honestly: the primary-level pass is a qualifying requirement, not a preference, and a secondary-level TET pass does not substitute for it. Second, use the correction window deliberately: after submitting, re-read the form for name spelling, category, qualification and photograph errors, and correct them by 7 November 2026 rather than discovering them at document verification. Third, prepare for the written examination on 3 and 4 December 2026 now, because the gap between the deadline and the examination is roughly a month, and that is the real preparation window. No agent can move a candidate past the deadline, and no payment outside the official portal is part of this recruitment. For readers in Nepal, the citizenship condition should be noted plainly: this is a Uttar Pradesh state recruitment for Indian citizens, and the official UPESSC portal is the only channel to trust. Candidates who meet the conditions have until 4 November 2026; after that date, the form closes.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Jagran Josh report on the UPESSC PRT deadline, published 3 November 2026.</small></p>
$$,
